title: 'Orca audit: process and IPC lessons for Gnomon'
summary: |-
  The founder asked what Gnomon can learn from stablyai/orca's inter-process communication and process handling. Three-lens audit: Arky (lifecycle), Aegis (trust) and a protocol reader.
  Adopt:
  - a descendant tree-kill with an unverifiable verdict;
  - socket ownership where "can't tell" is never treated as "dead" and the socket is never unlinked on close (Orca retired 23 race defects this way);
  - a readiness handshake and classified exit codes;
  - a deny-by-default permission tier on every RPC method;
  - tests for the deny-safe permission semantics;
  - backpressure handling.
  Adapt:
  - sessions that survive kernel updates (Gnomon's biggest spec gap);
  - journal-cursor catch-up;
  - ACP as a third backend;
  - a guide served by the binary;
  - fenced dispatch.
  Avoid:
  - the Agent SDK;
  - yolo bypasses and running agents without a sandbox;
  - unpinned agents;
  - static bearer tokens;
  - WebSockets without an Origin check;
  - screen-scrape status on the permission path.
  Open founder question: approving from a phone versus Secure Enclave presence.
symbols_touched:
  - '#session-runner'
  - '#supervisor'
  - $daemon-lifecycle
  - '#socket'
  - '#web-endpoint'
  - '#backend-adapter'
  - '#approval-broker'
